{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e3f4a1-9c2d-4f8e-a1b6-2d5e8f0a7c31",
    "name": "Express API Backend",
    "description": "Complete request collection for the Express backend in DevOps/api-backend.\n\nFolders: Auth, User, Products, Health & Misc.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Import this file into Postman.\n2. Select the \"Express API Backend - Local\" environment (or edit the baseUrl collection variable).\n3. Run the Auth folder first, in order: \"Register user\" then \"Login\". These store userId, loginEmail, loginPassword and authToken as collection variables.\n4. The User folder uses a Bearer token ({{authToken}}) at folder level; the public /greet request overrides it.\n5. Then run User, Products and Health & Misc. Every request has assertions in its Tests tab.\n\nNOTE: Login also sets an httpOnly accessToken cookie. Postman keeps that cookie in its jar, so protected requests work even without the Bearer header. The \"no token\" negative request clears the cookie explicitly to exercise the 401 branch.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:5001",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "authToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "registerEmail",
